  "details": "- CVE-2026-19445: ssl: resolve the SSLContext for the SNI servername callback\n  from the connection instead of the borrowed SSL_CTX argument, and unregister\n  the callback in context_dealloc, so a context dropped after sni_callback\n  switched the connection is no longer used after it is freed\n- CVE-2026-19553: ssl: validate SSLContext.wrap_bio() arguments in\n  SSLObject._create the way wrap_socket() does - reject server_hostname and\n  session in server mode, and emit a DeprecationWarning when check_hostname is\n  enabled but no server_hostname is given, surfacing the misconfiguration that\n  made certificate hostname verification be skipped silently",
